{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"gix-ref","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" 0.67.1 decides what to log, in its own source at ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gix-ref-0.67.1/src/store/file/transaction/commit.rs:51-62","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":":","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"code","language":"rust","text":"Target::Symbolic(_) => {\u000a    // Special HACK: no reflog for symref changes as there is no OID involved which the reflog needs.\u000a    // Unless, the ref is new and we can obtain a peeled id\u000a    // identified by the expectation of what could be there, as is the case when cloning.\u000a    match expected {\u000a        PreviousValue::ExistingMustMatch(Target::Object(oid)) => {\u000a            Some((Some(gix_hash::ObjectId::null(oid.kind())), oid))\u000a        }\u000a        _ => None,\u000a    }\u000a}"},"runs":[],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A reflog line needs two object ids; a symbolic target supplies neither, so the only symbolic update gix logs is the clone-shaped one, where the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"expectation","style":["emphasis"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" carries an oid. rc-git's expectations are ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"MustExistAndMatch(Target::Symbolic(..))","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for a previous branch, ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"MustExistAndMatch(Target::Object(..))","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for a previous detached commit, and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"MustExist","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" otherwise (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"checkout.rs:119-123","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") — a different ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"PreviousValue","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" variant from the one that logs, so no path through this edit reaches the writer. The switch does have both ids (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"HEAD","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"'s old commit and the target's tip), which is exactly why writing the line outside the transaction is possible at all.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Line::write_to","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" rather than a hand-rolled line.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" It is public (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gix-ref-0.67.1/src/store/file/log/line.rs:35","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") and documented as \"the git serialization format for ref log lines\", so the byte format — field order, oid encoding, signature and timestamp spelling, message escaping — stays gix's problem, not ours. The message text is git's own shape, ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"checkout: moving from <old> to <new>","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", because ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"git checkout -","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"git reflog","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" parse it; a friendlier message breaks both.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The synthetic ","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rc-git","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" / ","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rc-git@localhost","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" committer","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is the one every other rc-git ref edit uses (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Writer::apply_edit","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" → ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Writer::apply_edit_as","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/actions/write.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). Repositories open with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gix::open::Options::isolated()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", so no global config and no user identity is readable — there is nothing else to put in the signature.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Appending only when ","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"logs/HEAD","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" exists","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" matches ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"force_create_reflog: false","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" on the edit itself. Creating a log in a repository that has none would be a change the edit did not ask for and git did not make.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A missing previous commit becomes ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ObjectId::null","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" of the repository's hash kind, which is what git writes for an unborn starting point.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Prevention","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
