{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Route every \"move the working tree to another commit\" through ","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/actions/treeapply.rs","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", and move the ref last.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"plan","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"treeapply.rs:31","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") diffs the trees through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rc_git_core::Repository::diff_trees","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", splitting renames into a delete plus an add (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"treeapply.rs:81-94","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") and refusing submodules by name (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"treeapply.rs:197-201","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"); ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"verify_clean","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"treeapply.rs:111","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") refuses the whole operation with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ActionError::DirtyPath { path }","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for the first touched path that differs from ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"HEAD","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" on disk or in the index (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"treeapply.rs:128-150","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"); ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"apply","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"treeapply.rs:160","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") writes the files and updates the index for exactly those paths. Only then does the caller move its ref — the branch for a fast-forward pull (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/actions/remote/pull.rs:79-83","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"), ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"HEAD","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for the switch (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"checkout.rs:72-81","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). Ordering is the safety property: an interruption after the files land leaves visibly modified files on the branch the user started from, never something that looks like lost work.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The clippy write ban is the layer that has to list every door.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-core/tests/read_only.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" can only prove ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".git","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is byte-identical for the paths the lint actually covers; an unlisted write method means the lint passes while the guarantee is unenforced. Add the primitive to ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"clippy.toml","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in the same change that first uses it, and opt out at the call site with a reason so the exception is greppable — the test kit sat in the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"OpenOptions","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" gap for some time before the ban named it.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
